{
  "slug": "how-to-add-onedrive-to-windows-file-explorer",
  "title": "Missing OneDrive on Windows 11 PC, How to Add It to File Explorer?",
  "description": "Learn how to add OneDrive to File Explorer on Windows 10 and Windows 11. Follow setup steps and fix a OneDrive folder that is not showing in File Explorer.",
  "category": "PC Troubleshooting",
  "tags": [
    "Windows",
    "Cloud Storage",
    "How To",
    "Developer Tools"
  ],
  "url": "https://www.techtips.fun/blog/how-to-add-onedrive-to-windows-file-explorer/",
  "theme": "github-dark",
  "durationInFrames": 930,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "title": "Missing OneDrive on Windows 11 PC, How to Add It to File Explorer?",
      "subtitle": "Learn how to add OneDrive to File Explorer on Windows 10 and Windows 11.",
      "durationInFrames": 105
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Quick answer",
      "body": "To add OneDrive to File Explorer, install or open the OneDrive app, sign in with your Microsoft account, and complete OneDrive Setup.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "What you need to check before you start",
      "body": "You need a Windows 10 or Windows 11 PC with an internet connection. You also need a Microsoft personal account, work account, or school account.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Step 1: Download and install OneDrive manually",
      "body": "Download OneDrive from the official OneDrive download page, then install the app.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Step 2: Sign in to OneDrive",
      "body": "When OneDrive Setup opens, enter your Microsoft account email address and select Sign in.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Step 3: Select your preferred OneDrive folder location",
      "body": "OneDrive Setup shows the location for your OneDrive folder. Select Next to use the default location.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Step 4: Review Files On-Demand",
      "body": "OneDrive Setup explains Files On-Demand. This feature lets you see OneDrive files without downloading every file to your PC.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "outro",
      "heading": "Read the full article",
      "body": "New posts every week on the blog.",
      "url": "techtips.fun",
      "durationInFrames": 105
    }
  ],
